{
  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&nbsp;The proposed development would result in the loss of a family-sized dwellinghouse, the need for which is clearly demonstrated in the development plan and supporting evidence base. While it would provide a dwelling in the form of an HMO, it fails to demonstrate that this meets an identified need, and&nbsp; would not be located in an area with a high PTAL rating. As such, the proposal is considered to have a detrimental impact on the borough&#39;s housing supply and is contrary to the following policies:&nbsp;National Planning Policy Framework (December 2023)Policies&nbsp;D6, D14 and T4&nbsp;of the London Plan (March 2021)Policies SP3, SP8, DMD1, DMT1, DMH5 and DMSI3&nbsp;of the Barking and Dagenham Local Plan&nbsp;(September 2024)",
    "The proposal lacks clarity regarding the existing HMO on site regarding occupancy numbers number of bedrooms.&nbsp;The proposed HMO has the potential to increase the number of cars parking on the street, activity levels and coming and goings to and from the site leading to additional levels of noise and disturbance at the property and parking stress in the area. This is considered to have a negative impact on neighbouring amenity in this street of family housing and in turn the health and wellbeing of neighbouring residents.&nbsp;It is therefore considered contrary to:National Planning Policy Framework (December 2024)Policies&nbsp;GG3, D6, D14 and&nbsp;T6&nbsp;of the London Plan (March 2021)Policies DMT1 and&nbsp;DMT2 of the Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September 2024)"
  ],
